hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20972","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us from a man of the people of Sham called Ammar who said: We campaigned on the frontier a year then returned, and among us was an elder from Khatham, and al-Hajjaj was mentioned, so he fell into him and reviled him. I said to him: Why do you revile him while he fights the people of Iraq in obedience to the Commander of the Faithful. He said: He is the one who made them disbelieve. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: There will be five trials in this nation, four have passed and one remains, and it is the exterminating, and it is among you, O people of Sham. If you reach it, if you can be a stone then be so, and do not be with either of the two factions. Take a tunnel in the earth. Hammad said: And do not be. Hammad had narrated it to us before this. I said: Did you hear it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Yes. I said: May Allah have mercy upon you, did you not tell me that you saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that I ask you."
